(
  'pia', 'advanced', 'expert',
  'ALAKU, a deep offshore lease granted out of new acreage, 2025 to 2029',
  'Transitions and reading an outcome',
  'ALAKU, an Ekene synthetic deep offshore lease granted out of new acreage. One case file comes with this capstone: alaku_case.json carries the terms (cfg) and the production, capex and opex rows the engine ran, 2025 to 2029; paste it into the ledger view of the calculator. The terms: terrain deep_offshore, licence PML, lease new, no converted marginal field; a 20 percent working interest, and every money value is at that share; oil at 180 USD/bbl, gas at 3.4 USD/Mscf, every price flat; opex escalating at 0 percent a year from 2025; 60 percent of the gas used in-country; prior-year opex of 0 USD for the first year''s HCDT; 0 bbl produced before the ledger; the framework override auto, so each year is read under the law of its own year. Every other term is the engine''s default, which follows the texts: companies income tax at 30 percent, the NDDC levy at 3 percent of the total annual budget, the capital allowance over the five years the texts fix, the cost price ratio limit of 65 percent, the Sixth Schedule production allowance, and the tertiary education tax at its statutory rate. The royalty by price is read on the Petroleum Royalty Regulations 2022 base (the engine default). The Nigeria Tax Act 2025 leaves the deep offshore hydrocarbon tax rate open, so this capstone states the reading conservative_zero; none of the six values depends on it. A decommissioning sinking fund collects 90000000 USD at your share in equal contributions from the first year to the last, and the escrow condition of NTA s.86 is NOT met. Report six values: the total royalty in 2026, production royalty on liquids and gas plus the royalty by price; the hydrocarbon tax chargeable profit in 2026; the tertiary education tax in 2025; the development levy in 2027; companies income tax in 2028; and companies income tax over the life of the ledger. All six to six decimals.',
